From f209f2668bae614411ff03079f82dd58c7f77334 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kozz36 <vjose8506@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 18:29:21 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] feat(coding-agent): admit prepared Bash plans before
 native process creation

Bind real executor delegates through registered extension wrappers.
Evaluate the immutable final shell plan before spawning, retaining hard
blocks, configured confirmation, cancellation and context-loss rejection.
Keep native admission tests and SDK documentation with the gate.

Retained evidence: SDK scoped 172 tests plus the independent public
session-generation probe passed on the final candidate; no new campaign
or execution of this intermediate repository snapshot is claimed.
The live AgentSession merged-owner integration follows separately.
GP global remains RED and consultation causality remains UNKNOWN.
No host activation, publication, global install or P01 operation.

Risk: items 2 and 4 (authorization and invocation/concurrency isolation).
